MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because the Eric Clapton connection and relaxed blues sound match what I want to hear today.",
    "A Fool To Care and Slipstream fit my interest in rootsy, blues-oriented music, while the songwriting on Stranger To Stranger and Live at the Cellar Door gives me a reason to consider them another time."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Motown and O'Jays collections miss my current mood: interest in older music does not mean I want a soul hits compilation today.",
    "Early Beatles pop and a collection devoted to a particular Dylan period feel further from the relaxed blues listening I want, and I cannot judge The Definitive Collection without knowing the artist."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to lean too heavily on familiar veteran performers, even when their music serves a different listening mood.",
    "Several collections seem to assume that interest in established artists means I want hits packages or specialized archival releases."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to Old Sock matters most when it carries through to a relaxed blues sound, which makes The Breeze especially compelling.",
    "An album can suit my broader taste without being something I would choose now; I rarely pick more than one, and today I want a clear continuation of that blues mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my roots and blues interests but stretch them too broadly into classic pop, soul compilations, and specialized collections."
}
